The 2026 original survey states the precise question on pp219–220. The invariant is the full triple including the first k-invariant, not merely pi1 and pi2. The source asks for unmarked homotopy type of actual knot complements; peripheral and meridional data are not part of the stated invariant.

Lomonaco's original 1981 SectionX gives the quasi-aspherical completeness theorem and a relative finite-splitting description of the non-quasi-aspherical case. Every finitely-ended knot and every spun, twist-spun or fibered knot lies in the known subclass. Infinite-ended does not imply non-quasi-aspherical: Gonzalez-Acuna–Montesinos1983 specifically disproves that converse. The August2026 quandle paper has different first k-invariants and therefore does not refute Kirby4.36.

